# Insert Primatives — Project Structure

**Namespace spelling:** keep `Na__InsertPrimatives` / folder `InsertPrimatives`. Do not rename to Primitives. English UI may say Primitives.

**Loader** stays at Plugins root: `Na__InsertPrimatives__Loader__.rb`. It loads `01__AppCore` Reloader alone, then AppCore Main once at SketchUp startup. Tool commands / hotkeys only activate. After editing Ruby, use **Extensions → Na__InsertPrimitives → Reload Plugin Data** — never re-require the plugin from a tool shortcut. **Enable Dev Mode** at the bottom of that submenu writes `Na__DevMode__Enabled` in AppConfig JSON.

**Load order** lives in one file: `01__AppCore/Na__InsertPrimatives__AppCore__LoadManifest__.rb`. Update that list when adding a Ruby file. Do not add a second require/forget/reload list.

**DEVLOG** (`Na__InsertPrimatives__DEVLOG__.md`) stays at Modules root. Do not move or delete it.

## Numbered folders

- `01__AppCore` — PathResolver, LoadManifest, Main, Reloader, ModeSwitch
- `02__AppData` — `AppConfig__Main.json` (`Na__DevMode__Enabled`) + ConfigLoader; `UserConfig__Main.json` (menu placement) + UserConfigLoader (`Na__UserConfig__*`); ToolMemory (`Na__ToolMemory__*`, model attribute dictionary); persisted drawn-tool settings
- `03__AppUtils` — VCB parse, VCB arithmetic, format helpers, keyboard mixin
- `04__GeometryHelpers` — voxel grid, solids, roof geom, deep pick (hub + Focus/Pick/Context), slope, edge loops, quad rings (`Na__QuadRings__*`: walk a quad line's ring, measure its run, offset / array / divide it), profile sweep (`Na__ProfileSweep__*`: corner frame, plan, build and mitre for any edge profile)
- `05__PreviewGraphics` — cube wireframe (`Na__Preview__*`) and drawn previews (`Na__DrawnPreview__*`)
- `06__Tools__DrawnShared` — drag state machine mixin; shared revise for the modifier tools (`DrawnReviseShared` + `Watch` model observer + `Animate` ghost engine); `DrawnProfileSweepTool`, the mixin every profile tool includes after its own revise module; `DrawnLargeSelection` (`Na__LargeSelection__*`: the Yes / No / Cancel question before a tool takes on more than 10 preselected faces or 48 edges); `Camera__ParallelDrawingGuard` (`ParallelDrawingGuard`, prepended on Drawn Plane and Drawn Volume, and `Na__CameraGuard__*`: holds a parallel view's orientation against SketchUp 2027's Ctrl+Alt / AltGr orbit, middle mouse still orbits; popup option 2D Orbit Lock); `Camera__AltGrFilter` (`Na__AltGrFilter__*`: Windows thread hooks on SketchUp's UI thread that hide Ctrl+Alt from mouse messages while AltGr is held, so the 2027 orbit / pan never start and AltGr shortcuts still fire; on for the guarded tools, everywhere via Extensions > AltGr Never Orbits or Pans)
- `10__System__PlaceCube` — click-to-place cube tool and plane mode
- `20__System__DrawnPrimitives` — plane / volume / cylinder tools
- `21__System__DrawnRoofs` — pitched / hipped roof tools
- `22__System__DrawnStairs` — staircase: a DrawnVolumeTool subclass that adds a side stage and a flight stage after the block (tool, geometry, entry, preview)
- `30__System__DeepPushPull` — nested push/pull 3d + 2d (tool, commit, quad ring, revise, quad offset, follow: SHIFT+ALT every corner along its own edge, 2d pick, joint: a face on a smoothed surface (soft edges) pushes the WHOLE surface as one and preselected faces that share an edge push together — every face along its own normal, corners mitred (`Na__JointPush__*` geometry in JointGeometry: stretch the faces round it where they contain the travel, else rebuild with walls, a lone surface thickens; `na_jp__*` tool side in Joint). Option Joint Surfaces, on by default, SHIFT+TAB and a Shortcuts command; the 2D variant keeps one face)
- `31__System__DeepChamfer` — nested chamfer (tool, geometry, mitre, revise, preselect: loose edges selected before the tool starts are what it cuts, limit: the largest cut the faces allow and the eased drag, scrub: the drag opens at 25% of that limit, up for more, down for less, hotswap: Chamfer / Fillet / Ogee / Ovolo from the right-click menu, SHIFT+TAB (next profile) or their own Extensions commands pressed mid-cut keep the edges and the drag; no single letters, SketchUp's shortcuts take them first)
- `32__System__DeepOgee` — nested ogee moulding: a DrawnChamferTool subclass through the chamfer's `na_drawn__*` cut hooks, on the shared profile sweep (tool, geometry, revise)
- `33__System__DeepFillet` — nested fillet / radius, the same pattern (tool, geometry, revise). A new profile tool is its curve, its solve and its words — everything else is the profile sweep
- `34__System__DeepOvolo` — nested ovolo / cavetto: a quarter circle with a step, two values (radius,step: `40,5`, `40r` then `5`), TAB swaps convex and concave; step shoulders kept crisp through the sweep's `:hard_seams` (tool, geometry, revise)
- `35__System__DeepScale` — scale any group or component at any depth (double-click goes inside), or loose geometry / a multi-selection boxed in the open context's axes (no planes for those); dimensions are built in 3D, standing off along the object's own axes: grips filtered by Control Handles (bar + `scale_handles` option), dimensions you click and type into, and Stretch Planes saved on the definition — a grip on an axis with planes stretches the object AT the planes, so details keep their size (frame, field, commit, preview, planes, overlay, keys, tool). TAB About Centre, SHIFT+TAB Stretch Planes, CTRL offers a plane anywhere over the object; no single letters (SketchUp's shortcuts take them first), and every switch is a Shortcuts command under Deep Scale Options. The stretch edits every definition from inside its own context, one context at a time, as one undo step. Tool options may be `:toggle`, `:cycle` or `:action` (ToolOptions header)
- `36__System__DeepProject` — carry a face at any depth on to a target: a face's PLANE (each corner lands on it), a POINT (CTRL), or an OBJECT (SHIFT+TAB, first contact). Directions are the push tool's (normal, SHIFT slope, SHIFT+ALT follow, arrows) plus an edge (click it or DOWN; DOWN again flips). Every corner travels along a motion `m` with `m . normal = 1`, so a corner's journey is one height. Routes: follow, stretch (faces round it hold the travel), push (pushpull, start ring re-stitched, corners placed), loop cut (QUADS + into the solid). A target through the face CUTS AND EXTENDS (`:mixed`, follow or stretch only, never pushpull). VCB is an OFFSET (+ short, - past). Geometry is pure world maths (geometry, target, commit, revise, preview, tool)
- `37__System__DeepVertexMove` — the selection is the SCOPE: every vertex inside it at any depth is a candidate, nothing outside can move (started with nothing selected, it picks the scope first). Loose faces / edges in the selection ARE the pick: their corners are picked at once, and a scope step of only loose geometry needs no ENTER; groups and components still wait to be boxed (the safety catch). Welded curves touching a moving vertex are exploded, moved and welded back (`Na__CurveUnweld__*` in 04, also used by Deep Scale's stretch and uneven loose scale): SketchUp re-fits a curve round any vertex moved on its own. Box adds vertices, SHIFT+box / SHIFT+click removes, double-click a face takes its corners. The point cloud viewer's gimbal sits in the middle of the picks: arrows move along an axis, the centre square moves freely; snaps are Push/Pull's (grid travel, CTRL vertex, CTRL+SHIFT vertex then rounded); TAB swaps drawing axes / the axes of the group the picks share. A pick pressed and dragged moves the picks FROM that vertex (CTRL inference starts on it). ALT+drag the centre square places the BASE POINT (a 3D cursor) on a vertex without moving the picks; moves then measure from it, it travels with them, ESC / an undo / a new scope reset it; ALT is read from user32 at the press (`Na__CameraGuard__KeyDown?`), a bare ALT is swallowed while the gimbal is up, Ctrl+Alt passes (2027 orbit). Submenu: Visible Only (raytest per vertex, cached per camera; the squares filtered too, re-scanned when the camera settles), Vertex Size (log-scaled with zoom); in parallel views only, Depth Limit + Depth Plane (a box keeps what lies within the depth behind the picked face, or behind the box's front-most vertex) — the tool hides 2D-only options in its own `Na__DrawnMode__ToolOptions`. Unpicked vertices are muted red squares. Every point is world; the commit opens each context (`ExecuteInContext`), finds the picks again by world position, folds faces that would bend, and moves with `Na__SlopePush__MoveVertices` (scope, gimbal, commit, select, filters, base point, tool)
- `40__UserInterface` — right-click HtmlDialog (lifecycle/callbacks/placement + HTML builder). `UiIcons__MenuIcons__PrimitiveMenu/` holds one SVG per tool button (`Icon__InsertPrimitives__<Tool>__.svg`, #172b3a, stroke 34 on 1024, made with the vector-graphic-artist skill); `Na__RightClickPopup__IconFiles` in the HTML builder maps a mode key to its file, and each is inlined as a data URI (the popup is set_html, so a relative src has nothing to resolve against). A new tool adds a line there and an SVG here. The same folder holds the Noble Architecture logo shown across the top of the menu (`Na__InsertPrimatives__Brand__CompanyLogo__.svg`) and the NA mark (`..._Brand__CustomToolbarIcon__.svg`) on the loader's **Na Insert Primitives** launcher, an Extensions-menu command beside the submenu, because SketchUp gives a submenu no icon. **Menu Opens** (UserConfig `Na__RightClickMenu__ShowMode`: `right_click` default, or `with_tool`) keeps the menu open while any tool runs; `..._RightClickPopup__Persist__.rb`, LAST in the manifest, prepends an activate / deactivate reporter on every class that includes PrimitiveModeSwitching, so no tool has to call it. The menu's SIZE is the page's own (`reportLayout`: innerWidth/innerHeight, CSS px, stored as `Na__RightClickMenu__ContentSize` when the user's resize settles) and the window is steered to it on open; never round-trip `get_size` into `set_size` (different units), never let content grow the window (it scrolls), no `preferences_key`. Plane Faces is no longer a general button: it is the Face option (ToolOptions) under Plane and Drawn Plane

Filenames stay `Na__InsertPrimatives__<Domain>__<Purpose>__.rb`. Folder numbers do not appear in filenames.

**Config split:** `AppConfig__Main.json` is the plugin's own switches. `UserConfig__Main.json` is what the user arranged (menu anchor, position, size) and is written on every popup close. Do not mix the two.

**Retype / repeat contract:** a modifier tool includes `DrawnReviseShared` AFTER `DrawnToolShared`, then its own `Drawn<Tool>Revise` half. Host hooks are `na_revise__*` (memory key, parse, reacquire, rebuild, apply_repeat, draw_ghost, ghost_points). Tool memory is written INSIDE the placing operation only.

**Coordinate rule (SketchUp's, not ours):** in the active editing context and its parents every API coordinate is GLOBAL; inside any closed group it is LOCAL. View drawing, InputPoints and pick rays are always global — never convert preview points. PickHelper paths start at the active context: make them absolute with `Na__DeepPick__AbsolutePath` before `active_path=`, and use `transformation_at` as-is (identity for open-context entities). Entering a context flips its geometry to global: read-before-enter points go through `model.edit_transform` inside the block; read-after-enter points add with the identity. Full write-up in the DeepPick hub header and the 5.1.2 devlog.

## Naming and regions

- Module functions: `Na__Domain__FunctionName`
- Drawn-tool instance helpers: `na_drawn__*`
- Revise-contract instance helpers: `na_revise__*`
- Push/pull quad-offset instance helpers: `na_qo__*`
- Push/pull joint-surface instance helpers: `na_jp__*` (module functions `Na__JointPush__*`)
- Deep Scale instance helpers: `na_scale__*` (module functions `Na__ScaleFrame__*`, `Na__ScaleField__*`, `Na__ScalePlanes__*`, `Na__ScaleCommit__*`, `Na__ScalePreview__*`, `Na__ScaleVcb__*`)
- Deep Project instance helpers: `na_pj__*` (module functions `Na__Project__*`)
- SketchUp Tool API names stay unprefixed (`activate`, `onMouseMove`, `draw`)
- Tool class names stay `Drawn*Tool` / `PrimitiveCubeTool` (reloader markers depend on them)
- Regions use `# REGION | Name` / `# endregion`, not Visual Studio `#region`
- After extracting logic, leave `# @delegate: <relative path>` at the old site
